 panel.innerHTML=`<p>Allocate what you already have. Valid changes save as you type. Unassigned resources stay in Treasury. Military and Research receive these deliveries after the teacher completes this full round; they can spend them next planning round.</p><p><strong>Civilian food needed at retreats:</strong> ${state.territories.filter(t=>t.owner===active).reduce((n,t)=>n+t.foodNeed,0)} from Treasury. <strong>Military upkeep:</strong> ${living().filter(u=>u.country===active).length} food from its account after delivery. Keep food in both pools.</p><p><strong>Expected new production at current happiness:</strong> ${stockText(forecast)}. After current civilian needs and army upkeep, the food balance would be ${forecast.food-state.territories.filter(t=>t.owner===active).reduce((n,t)=>n+t.foodNeed,0)-living().filter(u=>u.country===active).length} per round, before recruitment. This arrives in Treasury at the end of the round, may change with captures, and cannot be allocated early.</p><div class="department-balances"><p><strong>Military can spend now</strong><br>${stockText(c.accounts.military)}</p><p><strong>Research can spend now</strong><br>${stockText(c.accounts.research)}</p></div><div class="allocation-list">${R.goods.map(g=>`<fieldset class="resource-allocation"><legend>${g} · ${pool[g]} to distribute</legend><div class="resource-allocation-body"><div class="allocation-art">${ResourceUI.icon(g)}<strong>${ResourceUI.names[g]}</strong></div><div class="allocation-fields"><label>Military <input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-dept="military" data-good="${g}" value="${c.allocations.military[g]}" ${locked?'disabled':''}></label><label>Research <input type="number" min="0" step="1" data-dept="research" data-good="${g}" value="${c.allocations.research[g]}" ${locked?'disabled':''}></label><p>Treasury reserve: <strong id="reserve-${g}">${c.stock[g]}</strong></p></div></div></fieldset>`).join('')}</div><p id="allocationStatus" role="status">${locked?'Allocations are locked until the next planning round.':'Valid entries save automatically. Enter 0 to return a pending allocation to Treasury.'}</p><h3>Your producing territories</h3><div>${state.territories.filter(t=>t.owner===active).map(t=>`<p>${esc(t.name)}: ${stockText(R.output(t))} · happiness ${t.happiness}/100 · needs ${t.foodNeed} food · ${t.deposit} mineral deposit</p>`).join('')||'<p>Capture territory to earn production.</p>'}</div>`;
